// Base64-encoded brand assets: Sean's Groundlayer logo, run through
// realfavicongenerator.net (2026-08-04) — a proper transparent-PNG pipeline,
// not the hand-rolled chroma-key attempt this file originally held. Served
// via dedicated cached routes (see index.js) rather than inlined as data
// URIs on every page, since these are real files (tens to ~120KB for the
// SVG) and inlining into 200+ pages' HTML would repeat that transfer on
// every request — a separate cacheable route lets the browser fetch each
// one once and reuse it site-wide.
//
// apple-touch-icon.png is used as the visible header logo (LOGO_HREF in
// templates.js), not one of the web-app-manifest-*.png files, because it's
// the only asset in this set with zero built-in padding (100% content
// coverage) — the web-app-manifest icons are PWA "maskable" icons with a
// deliberate ~17% safe-zone margin per the maskable-icon spec, which would
// make the header logo look small inside its 36x38 box.
//
// A faint grey mark near the icon's bottom-right (a leaf/flag-shaped notch,
// not random noise) appears consistently across every export Sean has
// provided — the original chat upload, the raw JPEG, and this generator
// output — which is strong evidence it's an intentional part of the source
// design rather than an export artifact. Left in place.

